seg-b49cbbca5b8e = One simplification matters more here than at Mars: the relays orbit inside Europa's Hill sphere (about { "13 700" } km) but Jupiter's pull on them is not modelled, so their orbits are idealised. The run shows the geometry and what the Earth link adds (availability rises from about half the Europan day to about three quarters), not a flyable design.

